    "answer": {
      "short": "$97$",
      "worked": "The general terms of the two expansions are\n$$T_{r+1}=\\binom{4}{r}2^r x^r,\\qquad U_{s+1}=\\binom{6}{s}(-1)^s x^{-2s}.$$\nTheir product contains $x^{r-2s}$. For the term independent of $x$,\n$$\\begin{aligned}r-2s&=0\\\\r&=2s.\\end{aligned}$$\nSince $0\\le r\\le4$ and $0\\le s\\le6$, the possible pairs are $(0,0)$, $(2,1)$ and $(4,2)$. Their contributions are\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\binom{4}{0}\\binom{6}{0}&=1,\\\\\\binom{4}{2}2^2\\binom{6}{1}(-1)^1&=-144,\\\\\\binom{4}{4}2^4\\binom{6}{2}(-1)^2&=240.\\end{aligned}$$\nHence the term independent of $x$ is\n$$1-144+240=97.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
